fast-lzma2 1.0.1 (tag v1.0.1 of https://github.com/conor42/fast-lzma2), unmodified
except for one patch, kept next to it: fl2-1.0.1-decoder-fixes.patch.

fl2-1.0.1-decoder-fixes.patch (since zpaq-std 65.4m-pre57; the third fix since
pre58) touches only lzma2_dec.c, the decoder; compressed bytes do not change. It is
the backport, by the maintainer of ultra-fast-lzma2 (a fork of fast-lzma2), of three
fixes made there (ultra-fast-lzma2 commits 5c2238c, d4f6342 and 2812bfc):
- a corrupt LZMA chunk could make the decoder read up to 20 bytes past the end of
  its input; the last bytes are now decoded from a zero-padded copy, as the LZMA
  SDK does;
- a chunk without properties after a dictionary reset was accepted, leaving pb
  uninitialized (shift by out-of-range amounts in C); it is now rejected, as the
  LZMA SDK does. It also fixes a typo in LZMA2_initDecoder (prop.lc = 2 where
  prop.pb = 2 was meant);
- an LZMA chunk that completed its output without consuming its whole packed size
  was accepted: the one-shot and single-threaded stream decoders stopped there and
  returned what they had, while the multi-threaded one read on. It is now rejected,
  as the LZMA SDK does.
Checked in zpaq-std: the reproducers of all three bugs are rejected under ASan and
UBSan, and -ma:flzma2 levels 1-10 (also with -m5 blocks) write and extract the
same bytes as before. Apply to a fresh v1.0.1 with:
    git apply --directory=compressors/fl2 compressors/fl2/fl2-1.0.1-decoder-fixes.patch
